- a way to define temporary variables for a proc (on the stack)?
- types must be defined before they are used
- .module or .namespace
- .obj, .objend
- .radix
- .type, .symtype
- .pushstate, .popstate
- .local
- variable-number-of-argument macros
- -W flag allowing more fine-grained control of warnings
- inlining function calls?
- a way to specify fixed-point numbers?
- .ifdef inside struct/union

Known defects:

- A user-type array field count defined after its instance can resolve to zero
  without rejecting an explicit initializer, emitting more than the declared
  structure size. Validate deferred counts before accepting the instance.
- Invalid named user-type array counts get a generic range diagnostic, even
  when defined before the structure with .equ, .define or =. Only literal and
  folded counts currently get the field-specific size diagnostic.
